{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"b5846eae7879a0289e577bf5c3019cf394792c01282846305c2cfad757fea555","digest":{"component_or_area":"op-cert inline-PEM configuration path","key_entities":["REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY","OpcertServiceConfig.from_env","_private_key_env","src/rebar/opcert_service/config.py","src/rebar/opcert_service/app.py","compose_signer","keyprov._validate_key_file","workspace._git","tests/unit/test_opcert_privkey_env_pop_932d.py","scripts/gen_env_registry.py","docs/env-vars.md"],"problem_keywords":["credential leakage","environment variable","secret management","process environment pollution","inline PEM","op-cert"],"propositions":["OpcertServiceConfig.from_env reads REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY from os.environ but never removes it, leaving the raw PEM exposed in process environment for the lifetime of the service","Child processes spawned after config load (ssh-keygen, git) inherit the unset inline PEM from os.environ because neither passes an explicit env parameter","_private_key_env should pop REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY after capturing its value to transfer the secret into the config object instead of copying it","The consume-once contract must be enforced: a second from_env() call in the same process yields private_key=None to prevent silent key loss if config reload is added in future","The pop must occur inside _private_key_env as a separate statement after os.environ.get to preserve env-var registry generation"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787718121129374001,"uuid":"e56e6efe-51cc-4f2a-8bca-89b4b58ca756"}